 of $t_P$ and $z$, each point in the diagram a single event. The metric is $L^2/z^2$ times Minkowski's, so the light rays are the lines of constant $t_P \\pm z$, at 45°.","The edge $z = 0$ is the boundary $\\sigma = 0$ of the global chart, and the chart covers the triangle $|t \\pm \\sigma| < \\pi$ beside it, with $t_P \\pm z = \\tan((t \\pm \\sigma)/2)$. The dilaton $\\phi = \\phi_h(1 + x\\arctan x)$ changes with $t_P$ and is least on the hyperbola $z^2 - t_P^2 = 1$, the middle of the wormhole. The marked rays cross it at $t_P = 0$ and leave the chart as $z \\to \\infty$, on their way to the other boundary."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"ab42a572ed410cac"},"slices":[{"view":"cylinder","surface":0,"label":"$t = 0$","version":"9eb330d03de5c381","lines":[[[0.1381,0.5],[0.8047,0.5]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.8047,0.5],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}],"thermal":[{"id":"radial","label":"$t_R$ and $\\rho$","plane":["t_R","\\rho"],"families":["ingoing","outgoing"],"xlabel":"$\\rho$","ylabel":"$t_R$","ticks":{"x":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"},{"at":2.5,"label":"$2.5$"},{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"}],"y":[{"at":-1.5,"label":"$-1.5$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-1$"},{"at":-0.5,"label":"$-0.5$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"}]},"box":[0,3,-1.5,1.5],"to_display":[[0.0,1.0],[1.0,0.0]],"mirror":false,"rays":{"P":[[[0.0357,-0.0214],[0.0276,0.0632],[0.021,0.1555],[0.0154,0.2578],[0.0109,0.3728],[0.0074,0.5002],[0.0048,0.6452],[0.0016,1.0202]],[[0.1068,-0.0205],[0.0943,0.0202],[0.0827,0.0636],[0.0719,0.1099],[0.0624,0.1564],[0.0538,0.2057],[0.046,0.2576],[0.0327,0.3718],[0.0223,0.4989],[0.0143,0.6462],[0.0086,0.8161],[0.0047,1.021]],[[0.1786,-0.021],[0.1576,0.0188],[0.1389,0.0597],[0.1213,0.1038],[0.1049,0.151